Examples:

Input: root[] = [10, 8, 2, 3, N, 3, 6, N, N, N, 4], k = 8

Output: 2
Explanation:
Cost For visiting Leaf Node 3: 3
Cost For visiting Leaf Node 4: 4
Cost For visiting Leaf Node 6: 3
To maximize the number of visited leaves, choose the two cheapest leaves: Cost = 3 + 3 = 6 ≤ 8. 
Thus, the maximum number of leaf nodes that can be visited is 2.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

class Solution {
  
    private void dfs(Node root, int level,int k, int freq[]){
        if(level>k) return;
        if(root==null) return;
        if(root.left==null && root.right==null){
            freq[level]++;
            return;
        }
        dfs(root.left,level+1,k,freq);
        dfs(root.right,level+1,k,freq);
    }
    
    public int getCount(Node root, int k) {
        // code here
        int freq[]= new int[k+1];
        dfs(root, 1,k,freq);
        
        int ans=0;
        int budget=k;
        
        for(int i=1;i<=k;i++){
            while(freq[i]>0 && budget>=i){
                budget-=i;
                ans++;
                freq[i]--;
            }
        }
        return ans;
    }
}
